Add a miniz ZIP backend to the xlsxio reader.

xlsxio 0.2.36 can drive minizip, minizip-ng or libzip, but not miniz, whose
ZIP reader has a different shape: there is no "current file" on the archive
handle, so an entry becomes an explicit extraction iterator. This patch adds
USE_MINIZ beside the existing backends and leaves them untouched.

  unzOpen()               ->  mz_zip_reader_init_file()
  unzLocateFile()         ->  mz_zip_reader_locate_file_v2(MZ_ZIP_FLAG_CASE_SENSITIVE)
  unzOpenCurrentFile()    ->  mz_zip_reader_extract_iter_new()
  unzReadCurrentFile()    ->  mz_zip_reader_extract_iter_read()
  unzCloseCurrentFile()   ->  mz_zip_reader_extract_iter_free()
  unzClose()              ->  mz_zip_reader_end()

Note mz_zip_reader_extract_iter_read() returns a size_t, so the minizip loop
condition "buflen >= 0" is vacuous for it and the read moves into the loop
body; a short read still ends the stream via the existing "done" test.

Origin: written in the utopp/pkg-xlsx prototype, reproduced here unchanged.
Applies to pristine xlsxio 0.2.36 src/vendor/xlsxio/lib/xlsxio_read.c.

